/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
.DS_Store

# Built locally by editors/vscode/install.ps1
*.vsix

# Everything `khora build`, `khora test` and `khora bench` make: the
# executable, its object file, a PDB on Windows, the `KHORA_EMIT_LLVM` dump.
#
# This was twenty lines. Output landed beside the source it came from, so every
# kind of file, in every tree that gets built, had to be named here --
# `examples/**/src/*.pdb`, `bench/**/src/*.o`, `**/khora-tests.exe.o` -- and
# the list was still incomplete: `std/khora-tests.exe` reached a commit, 3.5 MB
# of build output inside the standard library, because nothing here had named
# it. A `.gitignore` that has to grow every time the compiler learns to emit
# something is a compiler putting its output in the wrong place.
build/

# What the link shortener writes while it runs.
examples/**/links.txt

# `bench/control_keepalive.exe`, the control server `bench/README.md` builds
# with `rustc` rather than with `khora`.
bench/*.exe
bench/*.pdb

# Written by `scripts/setup-llvm.sh`; `.cargo/config.toml.example` is the
# template. It names an LLVM prefix and a Windows SDK version, both of which
# differ per machine.
/.cargo/config.toml

# The baseline's receipt. `scripts/baseline.sh` writes it on success and
# `scripts/gate.sh` reads it; it names a working tree, so it is meaningless on
# any other machine and belongs to nobody's history.
/.khora-gate-full
/.khora-gate-fast

# The peer servers `bench/measure.py` measures against, built by hand from
# `bench/peers/`. Sources are tracked; binaries and build trees are not.
/bench/peers/*.exe
/bench/peers/*.class
/bench/peers/dotnet_health/bin/
/bench/peers/dotnet_health/obj/
/bench/*/src/release.exe
/bench/*/src/release.exe.o
/bench/*/src/release.pdb
/bench/measure.json

# What `scripts/package.sh` assembles. Built on demand and published by the
# release workflow; never committed.
/dist/
__pycache__/
